course: dictionary
lesson: 6323
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word motion has several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one to use. Most often it means movement, the act of moving.
explain: «Rubbing your hands together makes them warm because friction turns motion into heat.» Here motion means movement. The clue is friction turning it into heat. Check by swapping in movement: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Motion can also be a verb, meaning to give someone a sign with your hand or head. It can also be a formal suggestion that a group votes on at a meeting. Context tells you which meaning you need.
explain: Phrases change the meaning too. «In slow motion» means moving very slowly. The tiny tardigrades in the moss are not rushing about; they are «plodding about like chubby bears in slow motion».
fact: Motion means movement, or the act of moving.
fact: Motion can mean a single movement, especially of the hand or body.
fact: As a verb, motion means to give someone a sign with your hand or head.
fact: In science, motion is studied with forces such as pushes and pulls.
fact: Motion sickness is feeling sick in a car, boat or plane.
exercise: «Rubbing your hands together makes them warm because friction turns motion into heat.» What does motion mean here? | *Movement | A bright light | A formal suggestion at a meeting | A sign made with the hand
exercise: Lena felt sick on the boat. Her mum says she has motion sickness. What is motion sickness? | Being sick in your sleep | *Feeling sick in a car, boat or plane | Feeling sick after eating too many sweets | A type of sea creature
exercise: «...plodding about like chubby bears in slow motion.» What does in slow motion mean? | Backwards | *Moving very slowly | Very quickly | Not moving at all
test: The class voted on the teacher's motion to have longer playtime. What is a motion here? | A type of car | A bright light | *A formal suggestion that a group votes on | A single movement of the hand
test: What does the phrase «go through the motions» suggest? | Standing perfectly still | *Doing something without really caring | Dancing very well | Running fast through a field
exam: «An automatic door uses a motion sensor to notice movement.» What does a motion sensor do? | Makes the door heavier | Keeps the door cold | Plays music | *Notices movement
